  clock: 4  # 33ee
  nonce: 33ee  # 33ee
  message: "CLAUSE-1 STATUS READ WITH THIS ITEM'S OWN INSTRUMENT (ci-debug logs\ncron/full-suite), which is the loop closing that the item was filed to\nenable.\n\nTHE CRON IS DOWN TO ONE FAILURE. At 8b55d1f4ef (08-16 01:00 UTC run):\n22,853 passed, 37 skipped, 17 xfailed, 1 FAILED —\ntest_run_behavior_map.py::test_pyproject_console_script_survives_and_is_detected_wi_papag,\ni.e. INV-kazij's test, exactly. The INV-vazuh install fixes (PR #349) held:\nrich present, packages installed, mypy fixture green. So clause 1 has\nnarrowed from \"the gate has never run\" through \"three install failures\" to\n\"one environment-conditional product test\".\n\nTREE EVIDENCE, measured: the failing run's tree (8b55d1f) is an ANCESTOR of\nthe tree the nightly matrix passed 4x (4e8c47e, all of 3.10/3.11/3.12/3.13\ngreen, full suite at 100% coverage). The window between them contains\nexactly the three climb PRs (#364 artifact scope, #365 stdlib climb, #366\noverlay climb) — none of which touches toml_config.py or entrypoints.py,\nthe detection path. Read honestly: the failure STOPPED EXPRESSING without\nits mechanism being fixed — consistent with an xdist ordering/collection\nshift — so INV-kazij is treated as LATENT, not cured (measurement posted\non that item).\n\nENVIRONMENT AXES ELIMINATED from the failing run's own log:\ntree-sitter-toml 0.7.0 installed in the failing container; tree-sitter\n0.25.2 == local; Python 3.11.14 (kills the filed \"3.10-only\" hypothesis).\nContainer reproduction locally is blocked: this box's agent user is not in\nthe docker group (documented, not worked around).\n\nCLAUSE-1 VERDICT PENDING: the next full-suite cron (13:00 UTC) fires on a\npost-climb tree for the first time. Nightly's 4-leg green at 4e8c47e is the\nprior. If it greens, clause 1 is satisfied ON THAT EVIDENCE (a green cron on\nthe tip, every reporting gate green) and this item can close — with\nINV-kazij explicitly NOT closed by it."  # 33ee
